e of the  square root you're gonna multiply by one  another and the ones that are on the  inside of the square root you're gonna  multiply those together so here we've  got 2 times 4 that's going to be 8  square root of 3 when we distribute to  this group we have 2 times negative 5 is  negative 10 square root of 3 times  square root of 3 is square root of 9 so  notice I multiplied the numbers on the  outside and then the square roots  together so like terms square root of 9  is 3 times 10 is  30 so we just get a square root of 3  minus 30 and you've got it okay number 4  we're multiplying a binomial 2 terms  times another binomial two terms so what  you can do is you can either use the  foil method or you can distribute twice  okay so let's go ahead and take do that  so 3 times 4 is 12 3 times 5 root 7 is  15 square root of 7 negative 2 root 5  times 4 is a negative 8 square root of 5  and then the last terms here we've got  negative 2 times 5 which is negative 10  square root of 5 times square root of 7  is square root of 35 now we look to see  if we can simplify further 35 is just 7  times 5 there's not a perfect square we  can divide out of that same thing here 5  is just 5 and 1 7 is just 7 and 1 so  that's as far as we can simplify there's  no you know like terms we can combine so  this is our final result and then the  last one number 5 we have a binomial  squared and what you do when you have a  binomial square is you can think of this  as 6 square root of 2 minus 9 and  another 6 square root of 2 minus 9 so  squaring you have that quantity twice  right so now we're gonna do the same  thing we did in this first example we're  going to distribute so we have 6 times 6  is 36 and notice whenever you multiply a  square root times itself the square root  of 2 times square to 2 you just get the  number underneath which is 2 you could  say square root of 4 which is 2 but I'll  just make that 2 so this is actually 72  6 times negative 9 is negative 54 and  the square